+# Homepage newsroom source map
+
+This change continues the existing homepage newsroom, rather than replacing its current editorial collection. Inspection began at Sites version 1071, commit `862014ab6edb2510093124cc806c4d6fc78fc529`. The live homepage already contained HomeBroadcastHeader, MettaSearch, InsightsTicker, NewsTicker and PsyNationRadio. The publishing source is the Sites repository for project `appgprj_6a93c8c170388191b89b2d90a544c0b1`; its current public domain is https://akashicnet.org.
+
+During the work, version 1072 / `b37723f30fb68e102f4e104911e9145d9b5d9867` added QCI content. Preserve that source when integrating this change.
+
+## Source authority
+
+The GitHub repository `tws9stmcbf-web/AkashicNET` was inspected at main `e342c8fea7ef6da7ffe2a5efa8fca17de72df6a4`. Its `website/` tree is a historical review snapshot. It has no current package manifest and its homepage is generated from `website/status-templates/home.tsx.in`. It is not the source used by the verified current Sites deployment. The earlier route ledger, `references/sites/akashicnet-org-route-sync-2026-09-14.json`, records the same separation. Open PR #403 also records later Sites publication separately from its proposed GitHub snapshot changes.
+
+Edit this checkout's `app/HomeBroadcastHeader.tsx`, `app/HomeNewsroomStories.tsx`, `app/MettaSearch.tsx` and associated modules for this feature. There is no homepage status-template generator in the authoritative Sites checkout. Do not copy the historical GitHub homepage over the deployed homepage or assume a GitHub merge publishes Sites. GitHub review can preserve the exact Sites patch and a deployment receipt without migrating unrelated routes, protected content or runtime configuration.
+
+## What changes
+
+- Reuse the existing branded logo and Pachamama newsroom artwork in a responsive lead panel. Retain the AI-art attribution and image-description access.
+- Keep InsightsTicker, the archive NewsTicker and the opt-in PsyNationRadio in the top broadcast panel. Their controls and privacy behaviour are unchanged.
+- Add a finite three-report evidence desk immediately after the broadcast panel, fed by the already-public `lib/newsroom-oct21.json` records. Retain report source, correction and bulletin dates and evidence/status wording verbatim. The selection is explicitly dated, without a real-time-news claim.
+- Extend the existing public page search with these report bodies. Support the public-page-and-report scope or featured-report-only scope. Preserve ranking, accent folding, additional results, clear-search focus and a focused results region. Announce only the result count, not the entire changing result list.
+- Preserve original article pages, source records, classifications and public-discovery exclusions. Search runs locally; no query telemetry or external search API is added.
+
+## Maintenance and checks
+
+The featured report adapter is an explicit public allowlist, not a crawl of all local files. When changing editions, update the adapter, its edition label and source record import together; confirm target anchors in the public newsroom. Keep source labels distinct from publication or correction dates. Do not treat selection for the homepage as evidence promotion.
+
+Run `npm run typecheck`, `node --test tests/home-newsroom.test.mjs`, the normal production build and `node --test tests/home-newsroom-rendered.test.mjs tests/akn24-rendered.test.mjs`. The build runs generated-ledger checks, public-route/asset checks, media capacity checks and sitemap privacy checks.
+
+Use a complete Git history before running the page-history generator. A shallow checkout makes the pre-existing generator misidentify the root commit as every page's first publication; those generated changes must not be released. Full history was retrieved for this work.
+
+The managed browser preview timed out at Vite startup twice. Browser interactions and phone/tablet screenshots are not verified by the production build or rendered HTML tests. CSS uses bounded grids and a single-column breakpoint; this is not a substitute for browser QA.
